{
  "summary": "This experiment tested transformer aggregation as a clean single-variable change from the prior best configuration (llm_summary_009: avgpool, ViT-L, weighted fusion), yielding a validation accuracy of 0.725 (F1 0.685) versus 0.706 (F1 0.667) for avgpool—a ~1.9-point accuracy gain. This gain is substantially larger than the ~0.3-point difference observed between transformer and avgpool in the RNA-only multiprofile regime (llm_summary_005 vs llm_summary_004), suggesting that in the multimodal setting the more expressive aggregation captures profile-level structure that better complements the ViT-L image signal under weighted fusion. It remains uncertain whether further aggregation tuning, alternative fusion strategies, or encoder scaling could yield additional gains, or whether the current configuration is approaching the achievable ceiling for this task."
}

